<td id="A2.T2.5.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.32</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Impact of Retriever Design</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The retriever serves as the first line of defense. Our comparison of three retrieval strategies in Table <a href="#A2.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ B.3 Impact of Retriever Design ‣ Appendix B Ablation Studies ‣ Quantifying Distributional Robustness of Agentic Tool-Selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> highlights a tension between relevance and robustness. Lexical retrieval (BM25) is the most brittle, while a hybrid approach offers a marginal improvement over purely semantic retrieval, confirming that retriever design is a critical component of the overall system’s security.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A2.T3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="A2.T3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Ablation on retriever variants.</span></figcaption>
